{"repo": {"timestamp": 1794652445000, "version": 20002, "name": "FPN Tunnel \u2014 AlienBoy69's repo", "icon": "icon.png", "address": "https://alienboy69.github.io/fdroid-repo/repo", "description": "FPN Tunnel releases signed by the developer. Add this repo to your F-Droid client to install and auto-update FPN Tunnel."}, "requests": {"install": [], "uninstall": []}, "apps": [{"antiFeatures": ["NonFreeNet"], "authorName": "AlienBoy69", "categories": ["Internet"], "changelog": "https://github.com/AlienBoy69/fpn-tunnel-android/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md", "suggestedVersionName": "4.5.1", "suggestedVersionCode": "24", "description": "FPN Tunnel is an unofficial, open-source client that turns a Mozilla VPN /\nFirefox Private Network subscription into a whole-device Android tunnel.\n\nSign in with your own Firefox account inside the app, pick an exit country\n(or let Auto race them and pick a healthy one), and the whole phone routes\nthrough Mozilla's MASQUE proxies. Built-in connection diagnostics (\"Doctor\")\ndetect sick gateways and fail over across countries automatically.\n\n* No root, no Termux, no companion app \u2014 a single APK\n* Native in-app Firefox account sign-in (no browser needed)\n* Multiple Mozilla accounts with one-tap switching\n* Tuned for filtered networks: DNS-over-HTTPS bootstrap, CONNECT-health\n  probing, cross-country failover\n* No ads, no analytics, no third-party trackers; anonymous error reporting\n  is off unless you opt in\n\nA small number of exit countries currently work without a subscription;\nthe full country set requires a paid Mozilla VPN / Firefox Private Network\nsubscription. Not affiliated with Mozilla.\n\nNote: builds from this repo are signed with the developer's key \u2014 the same\nkey as the GitHub release APKs, so updates work across both. They are NOT\ninterchangeable with the future official F-Droid build (signed by F-Droid).", "issueTracker": "https://github.com/AlienBoy69/fpn-tunnel-android/issues", "license": "MIT", "so